  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN218.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">tōḻi talaimakaḷai iṭattuyttup pakaṟkuṟi nērnta vāypāṭṭāṉ varaivu kaṭāyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante urged for marriage indirectly when granting a day tryst after having sent HER to the [designated] place.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN218.1">
        <l>kiḷaipā rāṭṭuṅ kaṭunaṭai vayakkaḷiṟu</l>
        <l>muḷaitaru pūṭṭi vēṇṭukuḷa karutta</l>
        <l>vāṇiṟa vuruvi ṉoḷiṟupu miṉṉip</l>
        <l>paruvuṟaip paḵṟuḷi citaṟi vāṉaviṉṟu</l>
        <l>peruvarai naḷircimai yatira vaṭṭittup<anchor n="1"/></l>
        <l>puyalē ṟuraiiya viyaliru ṇaṭunāḷ<anchor n="2"/></l>
        <l>viṟaliḻaip polinta kāṇpiṉ<anchor n="3"/> cāyaṟ</l>
        <l>ṟaṭaiit<anchor n="4"/> tiraṇṭaniṉ ṟōḷcērp pallataip</l>
        <l>paṭāa vākumeṅ kaṇṇeṉa nīyu</l>
        <l>miruṇmayaṅ kiyāmat tiyavukkeṭa vilaṅki</l>
        <l>varivayaṅ kirumpuli vaḻaṅkunīrp pārkkum</l>
        <l>perumalai viṭarakam varavari teṉṉāy</l>
        <l>varaveḷi tāka veṇṇuti yataṉā</l>
        <l><supplied>ṉu</supplied>ṇṇitiṟ kūṭṭiya paṭumā ṇāran</l>
        <l>taṇṇitu kamaḻu niṉmār porunā</l>
        <l>ḷaṭaiya muyaṅkē māyiṉ yāmum</l>
        <l>viṟaliḻai nekiḻac cāytu matuvē</l>
        <l>yaṉṉai yaṟiyiṉu maṟika valarvā</l>
        <l>yampaṉ mūtūr kēṭpiṉuṅ kēṭka</l>
        <l>vaṇṭiṟai koṇṭa verimaru ṭōṉṟa</l>
        <l>loṇpū vēṅkai kamaḻun</l>
        <l>taṇperuñ cāraṟ pakalvan tīmē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">“While the strong elephant bull with fast gait whom [its] kin praise,</l>
        <l corresp="2">brings sprouts [and] feeds [them], makes [them] eat herbs they want,</l>
        <l>the clouds, flashing brightly in the colour [and] shape of swords,</l>
        <l corresp="3f">scattering big drops, many drops, rumbling,</l>
        <l corresp="5">rolling so as to shake the cold summits of large mountains,</l>
        <l corresp="6">when thunder strokes clap in the rain, at midnight in broad darkness,</l>
        <l corresp="8">except for joining your plump round shoulders,</l>
        <l corresp="7">graceful to see, that glitter with victorious jewels,</l>
        <l corresp="9">nothing will happen to us”, saying so you,</l>
        <l corresp="12">without saying that coming is difficult within the caves in the big mountain,</l>
        <l corresp="10">where at midnight diffuse with darkness, lying across the path so it is lost,</l>
        <l corresp="11">the huge tiger glowing with stripes peers out for you wanderers,</l>
        <l corresp="13">consider coming to be easy, and therefore,</l>
        <l corresp="15d-16c">if one day we do not closely embrace</l>
        <l corresp="15a-c">your chest that coolly wafts</l>
        <l corresp="14">pounded glorious sandal that is finely mixed,</l>
        <l corresp="16d-17c">we too shall be emaciated, for [our] victorious jewels to become loose.</l>
        <l>That, even if mother knows, let her know. Even if</l>
        <l corresp="17d-19">the gossip-mouthed scandal[-happy] old village hears it, let them hear:</l>
        <l corresp="22">Come by day to the cool big slope,</l>
        <l corresp="21">where the kino tree is fragrant with flowers bright</l>
        <l corresp="20">in appearance as flames, that bees take for [their] seats.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
